3. PAPER-CUT ROW (Phase 14 disposition matrix: Re-scoped → W11)
================================================================================

### 3.1 Symptom (both scenarios)

  [init -> sponge-de] Warning: Libc RNG not configured
  [init -> sponge-de] Warning: ignoring unsupported RTLD_GLOBAL in dlopen()
  [init -> sponge-de] libEGL warning: MESA-LOADER: failed to retrieve
                     device information
  [init -> sponge-de] libEGL warning: failed to get driver name for fd 0
  [init -> sponge-de] Warning: flush page table entries - mapping cache
                      full - PD: init -> sponge-de out of CAP
  [init] child "sponge-de" requests resources: cap_quota=3

sponge-de then enters EGL/softpipe init and is killed by the cap
exhaustion. sponge_de_probe (in run/sponge-de-test.run) logs:

  [init -> sponge_de_probe] sponge-de-probe: capture poll 590
                            bg=0x1e1e2e demo=0x1e1e2e
  [init -> sponge_de_probe] Error: sponge-de-probe: FAIL rendering
                            never appeared on nitpicker
  [init] child "sponge_de_probe" exited with exit value 1
  Error: Test execution timed out

In run/sponge-launcher.run the launcher_probe installs hello fine
(`hello from package: running`), polls for the sponge-de launcher report,
but the report stays empty because sponge-de never rendered (its window
never came up after the CAP exhaustion). launcher_probe logs:

  [init -> launcher_probe] launcher-probe: poll 195 looking for
                           app='hello' cat='Utilities'
                           (launcher count=0) found=0
  [init -> launcher_probe] Error: launcher-probe: FAIL launcher report
                           never contained hello/Utilities
  [init] child "launcher_probe" exited with exit value 1
  Error: Test execution timed out

### 3.2 Root cause

base-sel4 capability accounting is roughly 3x base-linux's per operation
(each Genode capability maps to several raw seL4 caps). sponge-de's
Qt6/EGL init opens a large number of dataspace + pager sessions,
exhausts the per-PD cap quota, requests a tiny upgrade
(`upgrading quota donation for PD session (0 bytes, N caps)`), and then
blocks silently inside EGL/softpipe init. This is the documented
Phase 10 root cause in docs/09-roadmap.md §11.1 and is the EXACT same
pattern that the proven run/sponge-de-sel4-interactive.run already
worked around.

Reference proof (run/sponge-de-sel4-interactive.run lines 87-99):

  # Qt6/Mesa (EGL) on base-sel4 — RESOLVED (was: known limitation,
  # docs/09-roadmap.md §11.1): sponge-de's Qt6/EGL init used to block on
  # seL4. Root cause: capability exhaustion. base-sel4's cap accounting is
  # roughly 3x base-linux's per operation ... `caps: 1000` gives
  # comfortable headroom (measured: 300 hangs at EGL init; 1000 renders
  # the full desktop; RAM was never the bottleneck — the upgrade request
  # was 0 bytes, so `ram: 128M` matches the base-linux scenarios).

The cap-sizing fix is a one-line change per scenario
(`caps: 300` → `caps: 1000` on the `+ start sponge-de` line).

### 3.3 Disposition

  Item:       base-sel4 Qt6/Mesa cap sizing on sponge-de in test scenarios
  Symptom:    CAP exhaustion in EGL/softpipe init; scenarios cannot PASS.
  Repro:      `make -C genode/build/x86_64 run/sponge-de-test KERNEL=sel4
              BOARD=pc` (same after W1 staging fix); same for
              run/sponge-launcher.run.
  Root cause: Phase 10 §11.1 — base-sel4 per-PD cap accounting; sponge-de
              sized at the base-linux `caps: 300` instead of the proven
              base-sel4 `caps: 1000`.
  Fix shape:  one-line cap bump (300 → 1000) on the `+ start sponge-de`
              line of both run/sponge-de-test.run and run/sponge-launcher.run
              (matches the proven Phase 10 reference in
              run/sponge-de-sel4-interactive.run).
  Class:      Resolved in 14 (W11 paper-cut sweep; per W11 task #5/#13/#41
              pattern, trivial proven cap-sizing fixes are within W11 scope).
  W1 action:  RECORDED HERE; NOT APPLIED in W1 per the plan's explicit
              instruction (`do NOT silently fix it here`).

### 3.4 Verification path (for the W11 fix)

A separate trial run that bumps `caps: 300` to `caps: 1000` on the
`+ start sponge-de` line of both run scripts and re-runs the W1 make
invocations is expected to flip both scenarios to PASS within ~5 minutes
of wall-clock per scenario (the staging fix already packs the modules;
the cap bump only changes the per-PD quota). The W11 commit should
include both before/after receipts (this evidence + the post-fix log).

