4. run/sponge-configd-persist.run skeleton (W1 step 3)
================================================================================

A skeleton run scenario was authored per the W1 plan, building lib/ld +
core init sponge_configd + a tiny configd_probe and passing the full
[build_artifacts] list to build_boot_image. The scenario boots and
fails at the expected sentry (`configd-persist-probe: PASS` not yet
emitted — implementation arrives in W6 when the `<vfs>` persistence
activation lands in sponge_configd).

The skeleton's verification gate is a 30s timeout on the
`configd-persist-probe: PASS` regex. On the current tree (where
sponge_configd has no `<vfs>` activation) the probe logs nothing and
the run tool's run_genode_until times out, producing a bounded
failure that names exactly the W6 deliverable. The skeleton's PASS
marker is the W6 acceptance gate.

